From 207235c6fc7719f69622c6c5ae208cbbf116f3fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:44:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add optional extension for non-standard __exit__ argument
 names

Add the ``pylint.extensions.exit_argument_names`` extension with the
``non-standard-exit-argument-names`` (C3801) message. It is emitted when
the three arguments of ``__exit__`` or ``__aexit__`` are not named
``exc_type``, ``exc_value`` and ``traceback``, as in the Python data
model documentation.

Arguments matching ``ignored-argument-names``, signatures with
``*args``/``**kwargs``, static/class methods, nested functions and
signatures with the wrong arity are not checked.

Closes #7534
